.TH MSGRCV 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
msgrcv \- receive a System V message
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/msg.h>
.B ssize_t msgrcv(int id, void* message, size_t size, long type, int flags);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Receives a message selected by type into a buffer beginning with a long.
Size is the maximum text length, excluding the type.  Linux flags include
IPC_NOWAIT, MSG_NOERROR, MSG_EXCEPT and MSG_COPY.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of text bytes received, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR msgsnd (3crunch),
.BR msgrcv (2)
